  "description": "Wrap bold tags around all occurrences of words from a dictionary within a given string.",
  "target": "S = 'abccba', words = ['ab', 'ba']",
  "pseudocode": "1. mask = array of size S.length filled with false\n2. for word in words:\n3.   start = S.indexOf(word)\n4.   while start != -1:\n5.     for i from start to start + word.length - 1: mask[i] = true\n6.     start = S.indexOf(word, start + 1)\n7. res = ''\n8. for i from 0 to S.length:\n9.   if mask[i] and (i == 0 or !mask[i-1]): res += '<b>'\n10.  res += S[i]\n11.  if mask[i] and (i == S.length - 1 or !mask[i+1]): res += '</b>'",
